00:36:44.019 --> 00:36:45.780
it's received this replicated value

845
00:36:45.780 --> 00:36:49.760
and it's printed it out as 100, which is what we expect.

846
00:36:49.760 --> 00:36:56.309
And if I were to do that from the client,

847
00:36:56.309 --> 00:36:59.369
I press five, nothing is happening.

848
00:36:59.369 --> 00:37:02.510
And again, this is what we were talking about

849
00:37:02.510 --> 00:37:07.510
when the rep notify is only getting called

850
00:37:08.349 --> 00:37:10.210
when that value is replicated.

851
00:37:10.210 --> 00:37:12.829
And if you are setting it locally, it is not replicated.

852
00:37:12.829 --> 00:37:15.349
The same thing would apply for standalone.

853
00:37:15.349 --> 00:37:20.389
We can actually just test that.

854
00:37:20.389 --> 00:37:23.389
So wait for those other print strings to come in.

855
00:37:23.389 --> 00:37:24.789
So we're not getting confused.

856
00:37:24.789 --> 00:37:27.590
If I press five, I'm pressing five, nothing is happening.

857
00:37:27.590 --> 00:37:30.510
And that's not because the value isn't changing, it is,

858
00:37:30.510 --> 00:37:34.190
but our rep notify isn't firing

859
00:37:34.190 --> 00:37:35.949
because it's not getting replicated.

860
00:37:35.949 --> 00:37:37.010
When you set the value on a client,

861
00:37:37.010 --> 00:37:38.710
it's not replicating to anywhere.

862
00:37:38.710 --> 00:37:40.710
When you set the value in standalone mode,

863
00:37:40.710 --> 00:37:42.230
it's not replicating to anywhere.

864
00:37:42.230 --> 00:37:44.750
So you cannot trust on rep to get called

865
00:37:44.750 --> 00:37:49.050
in when that value is not replicated.

866
00:37:49.050 --> 00:37:50.670
And the only place it gets called

867
00:37:50.670 --> 00:37:52.349
is the place that it's getting replicated to.

868
00:37:52.349 --> 00:37:55.400
It will not get called on the server.

